label: Alert Assessment
description: >-
  One conclusion about the alert as a whole, reached from every entity's
  assessment at once. The gather's output — what the example could not express
  before `gather` existed, when a run ended with N Assessments and nothing able
  to say anything about the alert.
fields:
  entities:
    type: utf8
    label: Entities
    description: >-
      The entity ids this covers, sorted and joined. Deliberately carries no
      minLength: an alert naming nothing recognizable spreads to zero entities
      and gathers immediately to an empty collection, so the empty string is a
      real value here rather than a missing one.
    nullable: false
    validations:
      maxLength: 400
  entityCount:
    type: uint8
    label: Entity Count
    description: >-
      How many entities were assessed. Worth carrying rather than deriving from
      the string above: it is the one number that says the gather saw the whole
      collection, so a reader can tell a complete assessment from a partial one.
    nullable: false
    validations:
      min: 0
      max: 255
  summary:
    type: utf8
    label: Summary
    description: Every entity's verdict, in one line
    nullable: false
    validations:
      maxLength: 1000
